Diagnostic only. Measures where the thread that presents (the game's thread)
spends its time in Direct3D, with WINE_LOG=1 ("d3d-time" lines in wine.log):
- once per second: frames, calls, draws, the time inside Direct3D calls
  (outermost wined3d_mutex_lock to unlock, without waiting for the render
  thread), in wined3d_device_apply_stateblock(), waiting for command queue
  space, waiting for the queue to drain, and waiting at Present;
- every 5 s: the 15 callers of the lock with the most time (module+offset;
  resolve d3d9.dll offsets with addr2line on an unstripped d3d9.dll built from
  the same sources, image base 0x10000000), the time of each section of
  apply_stateblock and of each fixed-function branch with how often it ran,
  and push constant uploads by type;
- the steps of d3d9's DrawIndexedPrimitive, reported from
  IDirect3DDevice9::Present only, so not for games that present through the
  swapchain, as BO1 does.
Applies after 0019. Build wined3d.dll and d3d9.dll with it, install the
wined3d.dll in the runner and the d3d9.dll as d3d9.dll.orig (run.sh puts that
one in place at each start), and run with WINE_LOG=1.

